# Testing conventions

- Normal tests and CI are deterministic, secret-free, and network-free. They
  never call a live model provider.
- Test the Ask Diego endpoint through an injected fake HTTP transport and a
  fixed, synthetic corpus — not a fourth "mock provider" and not a real
  Groq/Gateway call.
- Any real-provider smoke test is manual, local-only tooling: never a merge
  gate, CI step, or fixture-update mechanism.
- Derive CV expectations by reading `content/source/cv.yaml` at test time;
  never commit a snapshot containing résumé/contact text.
- Cover manifest/schema rejection, bilingual content parity, honest
  project-state rendering, CV-sync provenance, corpus citation and
  "don't-know" behavior, prompt-injection resistance, oversized-body
  rejection, rate-limit and `402`/`429`/`503`/timeout fallback, and absence
  of secrets in build output.
- Serve E2E from the final build output with only the local origin allowed.
  Test keyboard operation, no-JavaScript content, `prefers-reduced-motion`,
  zoom/reflow, and automated WCAG 2.2 AA checks.
